# Fix 502 Bad Gateway and ExportPanel Prop Mismatch

The user is experiencing a "502 Bad Gateway" on `sqauto.zeraynce.com`. This indicates that Nginx is running but cannot connect to the Next.js application. Additionally, there is a React prop mismatch in the dashboard's `ExportPanel` component.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Fix React Prop Mismatch
Modify `ExportPanel.tsx` to accept the `disabled` prop and apply it to its buttons. This will resolve the TypeScript/React error on line 62 of `page.tsx`.

#### [MODIFY] [ExportPanel.tsx](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/components/ExportPanel.tsx)
- Add `interface ExportPanelProps { disabled?: boolean }`
- Update the component to use the prop.

### 2. Robust Proxy Headers for Nginx
Update the Nginx setup script to include standard proxy headers required for Cloudflare and modern web apps.

#### [MODIFY] [setup_nginx.sh](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/scripts/setup_nginx.sh)
- Add `X-Forwarded-For`, `X-Forwarded-Proto`, and `X-Real-IP` headers.
- Ensure `Host` header is correctly passed.

### 3. Production Configuration
Update the `.env` and Docker setup for a production environment.

#### [MODIFY] [.env](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/.env)
- Update `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` to use the actual domain `https://sqauto.zeraynce.com/api` instead of `localhost`.

#### [MODIFY] [docker-compose.yml](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/docker/docker-compose.yml)
- Change the `web` service command from `npm run dev:web` to a production-ready build/start sequence or ensure the current dev command is robust enough (though build/start is preferred).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **API URL Configuration**: I am updating `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` to `https://sqauto.zeraynce.com/api`. Please ensure that you have run the SSL setup (Certbot) as mentioned in your script, otherwise `https` might fail. If you haven't setup SSL yet, we should use `http://sqauto.zeraynce.com/api` temporarily.

> [!WARNING]
> **Port 3000 Connectivity**: The 502 error confirms Nginx is reaching the IP `4.230.17.169` but cannot find the app on port 3000. Please ensure your Docker containers are running on the server: `docker ps`.

## Open Questions
- Have you already run `sudo certbot --nginx -d sqauto.zeraynce.com` on the server?
- Is the SQAuto application intended to run on `4.230.17.169` or `4.230.18.242`? (Cloudflare points to `.169`).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- I will verify the code changes locally to ensure `ExportPanel` accepts the prop.
